So moving from X to Y we got thousands of people in our network that we support that we're going to

01:38.240 --> 01:40.690
have to go from x to y.

01:40.880 --> 01:42.830
So we can't flip the switch all at once.

01:42.830 --> 01:48.800
What we do is kind of a rolling release by department by department so our transition state would be

01:49.460 --> 01:55.530
some people are going to be on Windows y that we've made the transition for them.

01:55.670 --> 01:57.600
But other people are still on Windows x.

01:57.650 --> 02:03.800
So now we have dual support so that introduces some issues and some risk and maybe some you know some

02:03.800 --> 02:08.740
resource constraints that we have to consider in our project this transition stage.

02:08.960 --> 02:14.780
And then you know as more and more people come over to Windows Why is less and less of an issue and

02:14.780 --> 02:15.530
a risk.

